指，对理解实物遗存与荷马英雄世界的联系有用。  
- 摘录：  
  1. “The age of Homer was an age of heroes—Agamemnon, the king of Mycenae, 
Odysseus, the king of Ithaca, and Nestor, the king of Pylos, among others—whose 
deeds are chronicled in the Iliad and the Odyssey.”  
  2. “Many archaeologists believe that Homer’s tales, despite being composed 500
or more years after the Late Bronze Age events they describe, had roots in a 
real past. ‘There’s always a kernel of truth to stories handed down from 
generation to generation,’ says archaeologist Jack Davis.”  
  3. “Excavations at Pylos, and at sites all across mainland Greece, have 
provided a great deal of evidence of the Mycenaeans in their prime… they were 
tied into a world that encompassed most of the eastern Mediterranean, including 
ancient Egypt, the city-states of the Near East, and the islands of the 
Mediterranean.”  
  4. 
文中以狮鹫战士墓中的奢华随葬品（包括带有米诺斯风格图像的金印戒）为例，说明皮洛斯
精英在物质文化和象征体系上与米诺斯世界深度交织，并被视为理解荷马时代“尼斯托耳”形
象背后历史现实的重要证据。  

4.  
- 标题：Lord of the rings  
- URL：https://magazine.uc.edu/editors_picks/recent_features/lordoftherings.html
- 发布方/作者：University of Cincinnati Magazine；Rachel Richardson  
- 日期：2016年10月3日  
- 来源类型：大学杂志特写（面向公众的研究报道）  
- 触发查询语句：Ring of Nestor gold ring Pylos  
- 
相关性说明：以通俗方式叙述狮鹫战士墓及四枚金戒的发现过程、出土背景和研究团队的初
步解读，有助于构建发现史与考古现场叙述。  
- 摘录：  
  1. “When University of Cincinnati researchers uncovered the tomb of a Bronze 
Age warrior — left untouched for more than 3,500 years and packed with a 
spectacular array of precious jewelry, weapons and riches — the discovery was 
hailed by experts as ‘the find of a lifetime.’”  
  2. “New understandings of the artifacts — particularly the discovery of four 
golden rings — and the insights they provide to the origins of Greek 
civilization may prove to be the team's next big discovery.”  
  3. 
文章强调这批金戒在图像学上的复杂性：一枚戒指上的女神持镜场景与墓中发现的青铜镜相
互呼应，被解读为反映精英身份与宗教仪式的象征体系。  
  4. 
文中引用研究者观点，指出这些戒指及其它米诺斯风格物品表明早期迈锡尼精英不仅是战士
也可能是祭司或统治者，在构建后来的希腊文明叙事中具有重要地位。  

5.  
- 标题：Griffin Warrior Tomb  
- URL：https://griffinwarrior.org/griffin-warrior-tomb  
- 发布方/作者：Griffin Warrior project（University of Cincinnati 
相关项目网站）；Sharon Stocker, Jack Davis（文内署名）  
- 日期：约2019年（站点内容更新）  
- 来源类型：考古项目官方介绍页面  
- 触发查询语句：Ring of Nestor gold ring Pylos  
- 
相关性说明：提供墓葬的详细考古情境、物品分布和随葬品列表，包括对四枚金戒的简要点
名，可用于描述出土环境及其在皮洛斯精英墓葬中的组合意义。  
- 摘录：  
  1. “In May 2015 on the first day of renewed excavations at the palace, the 
team unexpectedly discovered a large, stone tomb. Hundreds of artifacts were 
found along with the body of a single male, the ‘Griffin Warrior.’”  
  2. “On the floor of the grave lay the skeleton of a single adult male 
surrounded by an enormous hoard of wealth… Gold cups rested on the warrior’s 
chest and stomach and by his right side were hundreds of carnelian, amethyst, 
amber, and gold beads.”  
  3. “A gold chain and a pendent, dozens of seal-stones carved with intricate 
designs, and four gold rings glittered beside him. A plaque of ivory with a 
representation of a griffon in a rocky landscape lay between the man’s legs. 
Nearby was a bronze mirror with an ivory handle.”  
  4. 文中说明该墓葬年代处于“the very beginning of Mycenaean 
civilization”，并指出随葬物品多为米诺斯风格或克里特制造，强调这位领袖在迈锡尼文
明形成初期的政治与文化角色。  

6.  
- 标题：Materialising Mythology. The Cup of Nestor from Shaft Grave IV at 
Mycenae  
- 
URL：https://www.researchgate.net/publication/337417728_Materialising_Mythology_
The_Cup_of_Nestor_from_Shaft_Grave_IV_at_Mycenae  
- 发布方/作者：学术论文托管于 ResearchGate（具体作者和期刊需通过论文获取）  
- 日期：2019  
- 来源类型：学术论文（考古学/古代史，讨论物质遗存与荷马神话）  
- 触发查询语句：Ring of Nestor significance Mycenaean Greece Homeric tradition 
archaeology literature  
- 
相关性说明：虽然主旨是“尼斯托耳之杯”，但论文聚焦于如何将迈锡尼实物与荷马文本中的
器物联系起来，讨论考古遗物被后世神话与史诗重新诠释的机制，可为“尼斯托耳之戒”与荷
马传统的解释提供理论框架与对比案例。  
- 摘录：  
  1. 
文章指出迈锡尼墓葬中的某些器物因后来的荷马史诗而获得新名称与叙事意义，强调物质文
化与文学传统之间并非简单对应，而是经由记忆与再解释形成。  
  2. 文中提到该杯与荷马文本中“尼斯托耳之杯”仅有“minor 
similarities”且缺乏明确考古平行物，用以警示将特定文物直接认定为史诗中具体物件的
风险。  
  3. 
作者分析迈锡尼精英墓葬中的器物组合与图像如何构建身份与权威，并探讨后世如何通过神
话将这些物品与著名英雄（如尼斯托耳）关联。  
  4. 
论文强调在解读任何“尼斯托耳”命名器物时需要谨慎区分考古证据与文学投射，这一方法论
可直接应用于关于“尼斯托耳之戒”的讨论。
