- 标题：The Lord of the Gold Rings: The Griffin Warrior of Pylos  
- URL：https://www.jstor.org/stable/10.2972/hesperia.85.4.0627.pdf  
- 发布方/作者：Jack L. Davis, Sharon R. Stocker；期刊 Hesperia（American School 
of Classical Studies at Athens）  
- 日期：2016  
- 来源类型：同行评审期刊文章（考古学）  
- 触发查询语句：Ring of Nestor gold ring Pylos  
- 
相关性说明：核心考古报告，详述皮洛斯“狮鹫战士”墓中四枚金印戒的出土、图像学和对迈
锡尼文化的意义，可用于建立“尼斯托耳之戒”在迈锡尼社会与仪式中的脉络并与荷马传统比
照。  
- 摘录：  
  1. “In May 2015, a University of Cincinnati team unexpectedly discovered a 
large stone-built tomb of Late Helladic IIA date near Tholos Tomb IV on the 
first day of renewed excavations at the Palace of Nestor, Pylos. Hundreds of 
artifacts of gold, silver, bronze, ivory, and semiprecious stones were found 
with the body of a single male, 30–35 years old, dubbed the ‘Griffin Warrior’.” 
  2. “Among the gold artifacts were four signet rings decorated with Minoan 
ritual scenes. Here we discuss the excavation of the grave, describe the rings, 
and consider the significance of the rings’ iconography for the Mycenaeans who 
buried them.”  
  3. 
（摘要概述）文章通过详细描绘戒指上的祭祀场景（女神、祭坛、树木、船只等），探讨这
些图像如何反映迈锡尼精英对米诺斯宗教与权力象征的接受与再语境化。  
  4. 
作者指出这批戒指的米诺斯风格与埋葬地点——尼斯托耳宫附近——共同表明晚期赫拉迪克早期
皮洛斯精英在政治与宗教观念上深度参与东地中海网络，对后来的迈锡尼宫殿社会具有基础
性意义。  

