detailed study of the so‑called Ring of Nestor (catalogued in CMS VI). The 
author explains that the paper is the product of many years of research on the 
ring and critically analyses its iconography, stylistic features, and 
archaeological documentation. Vlachopoulos explicitly refers to the object as 
the \"so‑called\" Ring of Nestor, signalling caution about its traditional 
