   Cretan–Mycenaean religion and royal symbolism. [18]                          
 • The Journal of Ancient Egyptian Interconnections article summarizes that the 
   “so-called Nestor Ring was found in 1924 and was accepted as authentic by Sir
   Arthur Evans whereas many other scholars condemned it as a forgery,”         
