   about the afterlife, emphasizing its sepulchral context and arguing that the 
   ring’s imagery is closely connected with the underworld, a chthonic or       
   afterlife goddess, or a journey of the soul, rather than primarily depicting 
   the authority or rituals of the living king. [21]                            
